# Every text file is LF on every checkout. Fixtures, golden vectors and embedded vectors are hashed
# and compared byte for byte, and git on Windows checks text out with CRLF by default: without this
# line a Windows checkout hands the tests other bytes than were committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Captured legacy volumes are bytes the current code wrote, read back by offset and by digest: an
# index points into a segment by byte offset, and a blob is named by the hash of its content. A
# checkout that converted line endings would hand the reader a volume no release ever wrote.
crates/*/tests/fixtures/legacy/** -text
